  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the Core Functions of Primary Care in Sub-Saharan Africa. - (PCAT) NA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">High-quality primary care, defined by five core functions (first-contact accessibility, continuity,
comprehensiveness, coordination, and people-centredness), is essential for achieving universal
health coverage in sub-Saharan Africa (SSA). However, health systems in the region lack
standardized, patient-centred tools to measure these functions, relying instead on fragmented,
disease-specific indicators. The Primary Care Assessment Tool (PCAT) has been adapted for SSA
and content-validated across 20 countries. This study will implement this newly validated regional
PCAT tool across 11 SSA countries to generate comparable data on primary care performance and
support evidence-based quality improvement.</narrative>
  </description>
